  "behavior_evidence": [
    "Nine Reserve cases compare size, capacity, storage identity, all move/copy/destructor callbacks, and final element values. Nonthrowing moves move all old values then destroy all moved-from old values; potentially throwing moves with copy support select copies; move-only native types select moves.",
    "Eight nextCapacity cases compare startup, maximum clamp, minimum beyond maximum, and usize doubling saturation using unmodified native headers with GCC -fno-access-control. Existing Reserve and new relocation adapter use the same Rust arithmetic helper.",
    "LocalArray storage states match the native protected isInline across default, inline growth, heap growth, retained empty heap, heap-to-inline relocation and Deallocate. No inline pointer or sizeof fabrication.",
    "Callback panic cleanup retains the old registered buffer/length and destroys partial replacement; this is tested as a Rust safety extension.",
    "Baseline compiler rejects both new callable adapters; candidate accepts/runs them. LinearVector Send/Sync/Unpin/unwind traits and covariance compile on both."
  ],
  "remaining_callable_work": [
    "LocalArray inlinePtr while heap-owned is not representable by SmallVec union storage without changing the actual representation. Native protected deallocate leaves dangling metadata; no weakened public alias was added.",
    "LinearVector automatic nontrivial growth for Append/Appended/EmplaceAppend/Resize/SetValue/Insert callers still uses Rust ownership moves unless a matching explicit relocation policy is supplied beforehand.",
    "LinearVector Erase still uses Vec removal rather than native move-assignment callbacks, and Insert still lacks native move-construction/destruction of each shifted slot. These are the next concrete method gaps.",
    "LinearVector move constructor has no explicit source-empty adapter yet, and move assignment still extracts source before receiver drop callbacks."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Explicit callbacks select the native move_if_noexcept branch; no automatic inference from Rust Clone/Drop traits or change to existing generic reserve behavior is claimed.",
    "The common native relocation domain requires minimum above current capacity, non-zero-sized movable non-self-referential values, and successful allocation/construction/drop.",
    "Native exceptions can leave leaked/unpublished storage; Rust partial-replacement cleanup is an extension, not native exception equivalence.",
    "Standard allocator identity, hooks, allocation-byte layout, trivial Standard::Reallocate in-place behavior and const writable Array1 aliases remain partial.",
    "Native private grow called directly with a non-growing minimum is outside the reserve adapter domain.",
    "No global API/test ledger was changed; compiler reachability and bounded rows do not prove class or whole-kernel parity."
  ],
